The portable C in the scenario setup-defaults: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/setup-defaults.txt,
see harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what
is expected in its place.
Deviation: 10, 14, 29 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the box of F10 names the program in its title and in its question, by a
name that is two letters shorter: the box is two cells narrower, a cell on
either side, and its shadow ends a cell further left. And the Advanced options
have no Quick execute commands: Clear keyboard buffer and what is below it in
the box stand a row further up, the cursor with them where it is on that box,
the box is a row shorter, and the two rows that its last row and the shadow
below it were on show what is behind the box, the upper one in the shadow. And
the setup's defaults sort the panels by name, where the original's are
unsorted: the setup file that Set default configuration writes has 0 for the
order of both panels where the original's has 8, and the program started on it
shows C:\WORK and the root of C: in the order of the names

